{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"The differential run exposed one required compatibility quirk in `stbds_hash_bytes`: the C code shifts an `unsigned char` through signed `int`, then sign-extends the low 32-bit word when bit 31 is set. Rust’s straightforward unsigned translation produced canonical SipHash instead of GCC’s actual output. I’m encoding that sign extension explicitly, which also preserves the original bug rather than “fixing” it."}}
